<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Forming and solving simultaneous equations of a rectangular garden</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The length and width of a rectangular garden are \(x\) metres and \(y\) metres. The length is \({@dd@}\) metres more than the width, and the area of the garden is \({@AA@}\ \mathrm{m}^2\).</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="A rectangle labelled x metres along its length and y metres along its width, with area {#AA#} square metres.">
[[jsxgraph width="320px" height="210px"]]
(function() {
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1, 7, 12.8, -1.5], axis:false, grid:false,
      keepaspectratio:true, showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false});
  b.create('polygon', [[0,0],[10,0],[10,5.5],[0,5.5]], {fillColor:'#a1d99b', fillOpacity:0.5,
      vertices:{visible:false}, borders:{strokeColor:'#2f6f2f', strokeWidth:2}, fixed:true});
  b.create('text', [5, -0.6, 'x m'], {anchorX:'middle', fontSize:16, fixed:true});
  b.create('text', [10.3, 2.75, 'y m'], {anchorX:'left', fontSize:16, fixed:true});
  b.create('text', [5, 2.75, 'Area = {#AA#} m²'], {anchorX:'middle', anchorY:'middle', fontSize:16, fixed:true});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>
<p><strong>a)</strong> Form two equations in \(x\) and \(y\) from this information.</p>
<div>Using the length and the width: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div>Using the area: [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p><strong>b)</strong> Solve the equations to find the dimensions of the garden.</p>
<div>Length \(x = \) [[input:ans3]] \(\mathrm{m}\) [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<div>Width \(y = \) [[input:ans4]] \(\mathrm{m}\) [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Each sentence of the problem gives one equation. "The length is \({@dd@}\) m more than the width" is a <strong>linear</strong> equation, and "the area is \({@AA@}\ \mathrm{m}^2\)" is a <strong>quadratic</strong> one:</p>
\[ x = y + {@dd@}, \qquad xy = {@AA@}. \]
<p>To solve a linear and a quadratic equation simultaneously, <strong>substitute</strong> the linear equation into the quadratic one. This gives a quadratic equation in one unknown:</p>
\[ \begin{align*} (y+{@dd@})\,y &= {@AA@}\\ {@y^2+dd*y-AA@} &= 0\\ {@(y-ww)*(y+LL)@} &= 0. \end{align*} \]
<p>So \(y = {@ww@}\) or \(y = {@-LL@}\). A width cannot be negative, so \(y = {@ww@}\), and then \(x = y + {@dd@} = {@LL@}\).</p>
<p>The garden is \({@LL@}\ \mathrm{m}\) long and \({@ww@}\ \mathrm{m}\) wide. Check: \({@LL@} \times {@ww@} = {@AA@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
